OHIRA-0010

Engineering Standards & Development Guide

Project: Ohira

Document ID: OHIRA-0010

Version: 1.0

Status: Founder's Draft


---

Purpose

This document establishes the engineering standards, workflows, and quality expectations for everyone contributing to Ohira.

Its goals are to:

Maintain a high-quality codebase.

Ensure consistency across packages.

Reduce technical debt.

Make onboarding contributors straightforward.

Enable predictable releases.



---

Engineering Principles

Simplicity First

Choose the simplest solution that satisfies the current requirements.

Avoid adding abstractions until there is a demonstrated need.


---

Modular Design

Each package should have one clear responsibility.

Packages communicate only through public interfaces.


---

Stable Public APIs

Public interfaces should remain stable across minor releases.

Breaking changes require a major version bump.


---

Test Before Merge

No feature is complete without automated tests.


---

Documentation Is Part of the Feature

Every new feature should include:

Code documentation

User documentation (when applicable)

API updates (if applicable)

Changelog entry



---

Technology Stack

Core language:

TypeScript (strict mode)


Runtime:

Node.js (Active LTS)


Package manager:

pnpm


Build system:

Turborepo


Testing:

Vitest


Linting:

